{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-15T12:45:27.037Z","data":{"text":"Task complete.\n\n**Summary**\n\nThe `osq query` output now builds a `recertifications` table after `pauses`.\n\n- New `src/core/report/query-recertifications.ts` exports `RECERTIFICATION_TABLES` and `insertRecertifications`, modeled on `query-pauses.ts`: reads each archived subject's digit-named task streams in numeric order through `readEventStream`, takes `data` with `asData`, and emits one row per attribution entry of every `recertification` event. `source` resolves to `measures`, `file_changed`, or null; `automatic` is 1 only when `data.automatic === true`; malformed events/entries/fields add no row or read null as specified.\n- `query-tables.ts` spreads `...RECERTIFICATION_TABLES` after `...PAUSE_TABLES` and calls `insertRecertifications` after `insertPauses`.\n- Updated the three full-table-list tests and the `query-pauses.test.ts` \"Pauses listed\" wording.\n- Added `tests/query-recertifications.test.ts` proving all four scenarios through the real `osq query` command.\n\nBoth the task verify (`tests/query-recertifications.test.ts`, 4/4) and the proposal verify (`pnpm verify`, exit 0) pass. Result written to `.run/results/3.md`."}}
